        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_INVENTORYM_INVENTORYITEMLOTSV2",
            "functionName": "getall_inventoryItemLots",
            "processJson": true,
            "name": "Get Lot Expiration"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772489366007"
          },
          "code": "GET_LOT_EXPIRATION",
          "id": "1769467838355",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772178454248_1",
              "name": "Query",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.EXPIRED_LOTS_PARAMS_BUILDER.$output.result.query}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1772178454249_2",
              "name": "Finder",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.EXPIRED_LOTS_PARAMS_BUILDER.$output.result.finder}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format Lot Expiration Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_LOT_EXPIRATION_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1769468250997",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769468250998_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Title/Header:** `Lot Expiration results:`\n\nYou are given:\n- **Expiration action results:** `{{$context.$nodes.GET_EXPIRATION_ACTION.$output}}`\n- **Quarantine Subinventory (if defined):** `{{$context.$nodes.QUARANTINE_SUBINVENTORY_CHECK.$output.ExpiredLotQuarantineSubinventory}}`\n- **Valid Material Status Codes:** `{{$context.$nodes.REDUCE_MATERIAL_STATUSES.$output.result}}`\n\n---\n\n## Output requirements (HTML)\n\n### Global HTML rules\n- Output **HTML only** (no Markdown tables or Markdown lists).\n- Do **not** wrap the output in `<pre>` or code blocks.\n- Ensure long sentences **wrap naturally** within the container:\n  - Use `style=\"white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: break-word;\"` on list containers and list items (or an enclosing `<div>`).\n- Keep section headings and ordering exactly as specified below.\n\n---\n\n## 1) Results table (HTML)\n- Render the results as an **HTML `<table>`**.\n- Columns (exactly these, in this order):\n  1. `LotNumber`\n  2. `ItemNumber`\n  3. `Subinventory`\n  4. `OrganizationCode`\n  5. `Expiration Date`\n  6. `LPN ID`\n  7. `Locator`\n- Use `<thead>` and `<tbody>`.\n- Use light, readable styling (borders + padding) via inline styles (since external CSS may not be available).\n  - Example styles are allowed (borders, padding, background for header row), but keep it minimal/clean.\n\n### 2) Skip empty records\n- Do **not** output any table row or recommendation for a record where `lotNumber` is blank **OR** `itemNumber` is blank.\n\n---\n\n## 3) End-of-output sections (after the table), in this exact order:\n\n### A) Recommendations\n- Render recommendations as a **nested HTML list** that is visually clean and wraps well:\n  - Outer list: `<ol>`\n  - Inner list: `<ul>`\n- For each valid record, create one `<li>` in the outer `<ol>`.\n  - In that outer `<li>`, include a short record label line (example: `Lot <lotNumber> / Item <itemNumber> / Subinventory <subinventory> / Org <orgcode>`) in a `<div>` (optional but preferred for readability).\n  - Under it, include an inner `<ul>` with **exactly two `<li>` items**, one per recommendation template:\n    1) Movement Request recommendation (template)\n    2) Material Status Update recommendation (template)\n- **Each recommendation must be its own `<li>`** (do not combine both recommendations into one line).\n- DO NOT show recommendations for the lot with expiration date in the future(today's date: {{$context.$system.$currentDate ).\n\n#### Placeholders (must be literal tokens, not escaped)\n- Destination sub placeholder token: `[insert the destination subinventory here]`\n- Material status placeholder token: `[insert the material status code here]`\n- Output them **exactly** as shown above (no backslashes, no escaping brackets).\n\n#### Highlighting (HTML)\n- If `expirationAction` is **valid and present** for that record, highlight **ONLY** the matching inner `<li>` using HTML bold:\n  - Wrap only that recommendation sentence with `<strong>...</strong>`\n  - Additionally, append the **description** from the record at the **end of the same highlighted recommendation line**, formatted **exactly** as *(Expiration Action: description)*, in **parentheses** and **cursive**:\n    - Append: `<em>(Expiration Action: <description>)</em>`\n    - This parenthesized cursive text must appear **only** on the highlighted recommendation line.\n- Valid actions mapping:\n  - If action indicates **movement request** ⇒ bold the movement request recommendation.\n  - If action indicates **material status update** ⇒ bold the material status update recommendation.\n\n#### Use these exact recommendation texts (verbatim except for substituting record values)\n**Movement Request recommendation (template; include locator/lpn only when they have a non-null, non-empty value)**\n\nBase template (no optional fields):\nCreate a movement request for item <itemNumber>, in subinventory <subinventory>, and organization <orgcode>, of lot <lotNumber>, to the destination subinventory [insert the destination subinventory here] of quantity <onhandquantity> <UOM>.\nOptional append (add only if present):\n- If <locator> is not null/empty: append Locator <locator>.\n- If <lpn> is not null/empty: append LPN <lpn>.\n\nSingle-line “all-in-one” version (with conditional segments):\nCreate a movement request for item <itemNumber>, in subinventory <subinventory>, and organization <orgcode>, of lot <lotNumber>[, locator <locator>][, lpn <lpn>] to the destination subinventory [insert the destination subinventory here] of quantity <onhandquantity> <UOM>.\nInclude [, locator <locator>] only if <locator> has a valid value (not null/empty).\nInclude [, lpn <lpn>] only if <lpn> has a valid value (not null/empty).\n\n**Material Status Update recommendation (template)**\n- `Update the material status for the lot <lotNumber> from organization <organizationName> for the item <itemNumber> to [insert the material status code here].`\n\n#### Wrapping requirement for recommendations\n- Apply wrapping-friendly inline style at least once on the recommendations container (preferred) and/or each `<li>`, e.g.:\n  - `style=\"white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: break-word;\"`\n\n---\n\n### B) Quarantine Subinventory\n- Output a section header: `B) Quarantine Subinventory` using an HTML heading tag (e.g., `<h3>`).\n- Then output exactly one line beneath it in a `<div>` or `<p>`:\n  - If `ExpiredLotQuarantineSubinventory` is present and valid:\n    - `Quarantine Subinventory: <value>`\n  - Otherwise:\n    - `Quarantine Subinventory: No quarantine subinventory defined`\n\n---\n\n### C) Material status code (valid values) \n- Insert a **blank line** between sections B and C (in HTML, use either an empty `<div>` with margin or a `<br>`).\n- Output a section header: `C) Material status code (valid values):` using an HTML heading tag (e.g., `<h3>`).\n- Then render the list from `{{$context.$nodes.REDUCE_MATERIAL_STATUSES.$output.result}}` as an HTML `<ul>` with one `<li>` per status code.\n\n---\n\n## Formatting rules\n- Keep the output clean and readable.\n- Use consistent labels and ordering as specified above.\n- Do not introduce extra sections or reorder anything."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
