          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769712174325_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Based on the following prompt: \" {{$context.$variables.UserQuery}}\", \n1. Calculate a expiration range and set:\nExpirationStartDate in format 'YYYY-MM-DD'.\nExpirationEndDate in format 'YYYY-MM-DD'.\n\nIf the user is searching expired lots without specifying any exact date, then set ExpirationStartDate with today's date( {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}), and ExpirationEndDate relative to today's date(in case that a relative date range like 2 months is mentioned, otherwise leave it as '').\nIf it is not possible to calculate ExpirationStartDate the value will be ''.\nIf it is not possible to calculate ExpirationEndDate the value will be ''.\n\n2. Get Lot Number\nUnless explicitly mentioned do not set the LotNumber, some other attributes could also have lot as a part of their name. User will explicitly mention if he is passing the LotNumber, otherwise set it as an empty string ''.\nOutput Format:\n{\n  \"LotNumber\": \"<lot number>\",\n  \"ExpirationStartDate\": \"<date>\",\n  \"ExpirationEndDate\": <date>\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"ExpirationEndDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ExpirationStartDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"LotNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
