                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1772154057212"
                  },
                  "code": "CREATE_RECOMMENDATIONS",
                  "id": "1772157024755",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772157024756_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "First display the list of demands in the same organization for the item, and then display the lots along with their locator, subinventoryCode, OnhandQuantity then suggest user that they can reserve the item <ItemNumber> from organization <OrganizationCode> with appropriate lotNumber and quantity(here it should be the quantity of the demand) displayed above. \nThen mention the fact that it won't be enough to address all the items in the expiring lots so show a list of orgs with demand quantity available in each one. Then suggest the user to create an interorganization transfer request for item <ItemNumber> from organization <OrganizationCode> with the lots mentioned above. DO NOT mention the same organization code as one of the orgs available for interorg transfer.\n\nNote: Your goal here is to create on optimal plan for suggestions that are explicit in details.\nFor the reservation suggestion, it should have the itemNumber, OrganizationCode, Demand Type, OrderIdentifier of demand, along with the Demand quantity. \nEx: Create Reservation for item <ItemNumber>, in Organization <OrganizationCode>, Subinventory <SubinventoryCode> and Lot <LotNumber>, with the <Demand Type> Demand <Order Identifier> with quantity <Quantity>.\nFor interorg transfer request, we need itemNumber, OrganizationCode, LotNumber, SubinventoryCode, DestinationOrganizationCode(from the Organization and total demand details), and the quantity.\nEx: Create an inter-organization transfer transaction with item  <ItemNumber>, in Organization <OrganizationCode>, Subinventory <SubinventoryCode>, Locator<Locator> and Lot <LotNumber>, into the destination organization <DestOrganizationCode> with quantity <quantity>.\n\nNotes for output:\nDo not include any notes or verbose explanation in the output. Output should only present the data followed by suggestions. Keep the explanation to a bare minimum(one line) and at the end.\n\nOutput Format:\n** Item Number <ItemNumber>\n** Same Organization Demand Details\n** Expiring Lots\n** Reservation Suggestions\n** Other Organization Demands(Exclude the current OrganizationCode from this list)\n** Inter-Organization Transfer Transaction Request\n** Final Note(Rationale for the plan)\n\n- Demand Details for the same org:  {{$context.$nodes.ITEM_ITERATOR.SAME_ORG_DEMAND_FILTER.$output.result}} \n- Organization and Total Demand Details: {{$context.$variables.LotOrgMap[$context.$nodes.ITEM_ITERATOR.$currentItem]}}\n- Lot Details: {{$context.$variables.LotItemMap[$context.$nodes.ITEM_ITERATOR.$currentItem].lot}} \n- OrganizationCode: {{$context.$variables.OrganizationCode}}\n- ItemNumber: {{$context.$variables.LotItemMap[$context.$nodes.ITEM_ITERATOR.$currentItem].item}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Construct Same Org Recommendations"
